This is how the user changes Persona's settings: ask them in conversation, there is no settings page for these. `list` (the default) shows every key with a one-line description, how to set it and its current value (secrets only as set or unset); `get` reads one. `set`, `add` and `remove` show before → after as a confirmation card in Persona and change nothing until they approve; secrets are entered there, never in chat. Change only what was asked. Areas: assistant behavior, session triage, About Me, saved prompts, start page and sidebar, inbox sorting and task links, mail accounts, extensions (`extension.<id>`, channels and connectors too: its own switch, `enabled`, and its settings) and their download mirrors, hub updates, device notifications, each agent CLI's settings per computer and muted Claude config directories. Model profiles are not here: use `model_profiles_list`.

`test` checks a provider ID for a `model_config.*` group, without approval or saving. `assistant.standing_authorizations`: never invent a quote or widen a grant's scope, and give only conditions that can be checked independently.

Details: read .claude/skills/persona-work/references/persona-settings.md in your working directory.